      },
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 8.06,
          "en": "Now with all these bindings you hopefully got an overview of how you can work with Svelte",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 8.06,
          "end": 12.72,
          "en": "and its bindings to conveniently get access to form values and using two-way binding here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.72,
          "end": 16.9,
          "en": "really is extremely helpful and you'll often use it when working with forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 17.88,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "There is another way of getting access to any element on the page though, so besides using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 26.74,
          "en": "two-way binding and also not limited to inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 27.32,
          "end": 31.4,
          "en": "let me first demonstrate it with the help of an input though let's say here we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 31.4,
          "end": 32.92,
          "en": "have an input and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 32.92,
          "end": 37.42,
          "en": "we have a button and I only need the value once I clicked that button so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 37.42,
          "end": 41.64,
          "en": "here in on:click I'll",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 41.64,
          "end": 47.06,
          "en": "trigger saveData which is a function I have yet to add so let's do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 47.06,
          "end": 48.88,
          "en": "quickly here we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 50.34,
          "end": 55.36,
          "en": "saveData and I'm not accepting any event object in here because that would be my",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 55.36,
          "end": 59.2,
          "en": "click event and I'm not interested in that but I do want to get the text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 59.2,
          "end": 60.3,
          "en": "that was entered into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 60.3,
          "end": 66.8,
          "en": "this input. Of course we could set up two-way binding with bind:value and then storing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 66.8,
          "end": 71.62,
          "en": "data which is in that input in some variable. But if I only need this in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 71.62,
          "end": 73.24,
          "en": "a read-only way and I never",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 73.24,
          "end": 76.94,
          "en": "set the value anywhere else I could do it and it would not be wrong and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 76.94,
          "end": 78,
          "en": "in most cases you will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 83.98,
          "en": "probably do it with two-way binding but you can actually also simply read the value from the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 83.98,
          "end": 90.7,
          "en": "So of course, what we could do here is we could console.log, document.querySelector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 91.34,
          "end": 96.36,
          "en": "and then maybe give this some ID, username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 96.96000000000001,
          "end": 99.47999999999999,
          "en": "So hashtag username selects by ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 99.8,
          "end": 103.92,
          "en": "Let's now give this here the ID, username, so that this is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 104.28,
          "end": 106.36,
          "en": "And now we get access to this element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 106.36,
          "end": 110.86,
          "en": "And since it's input element, this will have a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 111.38,
          "end": 113.53999999999999,
          "en": "And if we do that and we save that all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 113.74000000000001,
          "end": 117.44,
          "en": "and I enter super or whatever you want here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 119.32,
          "en": "and I click save, you see that being printed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 119.75999999999999,
          "end": 122.68,
          "en": "This is not the svelte-ish way of doing it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 122.98,
          "end": 126.52,
          "en": "This is vanilla JavaScript code, which you can use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 126.68,
          "end": 128.34,
          "en": "but there's a more elegant solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 128.56,
          "end": 131.4,
          "en": "And you might remember that I used a similar approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 131.4,
          "end": 133.96,
          "en": "earlier in the course where I also used querySelector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 133.96,
          "end": 136.64,
          "en": "because I had no better tool for the job.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 137.36,
          "end": 139.12,
          "en": "Now, actually, there is a better tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 139.12,
          "end": 142.57999999999998,
          "en": "You can use binding, but a special form of binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 143.24,
          "end": 146,
          "en": "So instead of relying on selecting this by ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 147.22,
          "end": 148.86,
          "en": "you can instead add bind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 148.98,
          "end": 150.57999999999998,
          "en": "but now you don't bind to value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 150.57999999999998,
          "end": 153.48,
          "en": "because I don't want two-way binding, but to this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 153.68,
          "end": 157.06,
          "en": "which is simply a special syntax understood by Svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 157.24,
          "end": 160.18,
          "en": "This thing here is not a normal attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 160.18,
          "end": 161.56,
          "en": "you could add to an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 161.74,
          "end": 163.9,
          "en": "This is simply understood by the Svelte compiler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 164.16,
          "end": 165.8,
          "en": "And by binding to this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.8,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "you can store a reference to that element here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 169.96,
          "end": 173.04,
          "en": "a pointer to that element in a variable of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 173.44,
          "end": 175.6,
          "en": "So now we can add a new variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 176.3,
          "end": 177.84,
          "en": "usernameInput, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 178.46,
          "end": 182.72,
          "en": "And this is the variable which I'll use down there, usernameInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183.04,
          "end": 186.26,
          "en": "So now a pointer at this HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 186.26,
          "end": 188.86,
          "en": "or at this DOM element, to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.18,
          "end": 191.4,
          "en": "is stored in usernameInput.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 191.8,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "And therefore here in saveData,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 198.8,
          "en": "I can now console.log usernameInput.value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.8,
          "end": 201.34,
          "en": "because this points at this HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.78,
          "end": 205.02,
          "en": "And hence now if I enter super here and I click save,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.66,
          "end": 207.06,
          "en": "you see that still works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 207.22,
          "end": 208.78,
          "en": "but of course that's way shorter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.78,
          "end": 211.24,
          "en": "than manually selecting this with querySelector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.48,
          "end": 213.92000000000002,
          "en": "And we also don't have to add the ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.12,
          "end": 214.94,
          "en": "We can remove that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.94,
          "end": 217.52,
          "en": "because now this reference and connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 217.52,
          "end": 219.7,
          "en": "is set up behind the scenes by Svelte.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.98,
          "end": 221.54,
          "en": "Now this is not two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.74,
          "end": 223.98,
          "en": "This is really just a pointer at the full element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.16,
          "end": 226.38,
          "en": "We're not restricted to reading its value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.57999999999998,
          "end": 227.74,
          "en": "We can do whatever we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 227.88,
          "end": 230.9,
          "en": "We can manipulate it, though I would not recommend that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.1,
          "end": 233.14,
          "en": "You shouldn't change it programmatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.14,
          "end": 236.46,
          "en": "You should always change your DOM through Svelte",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.46,
          "end": 238.22,
          "en": "by the instructions you place down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.42000000000002,
          "end": 240.64,
          "en": "But you can read any data you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.82,
          "end": 243.24,
          "en": "You can check out the CSS classes on the element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.4,
          "end": 246.04,
          "en": "You can do whatever you want because if we log it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.14,
          "end": 247.9,
          "en": "you'll see it's just a full element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.18,
          "end": 252.34,
          "en": "So if a console log this here, and I press save again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.5,
          "end": 253.56,
          "en": "it's the full input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.16,
          "end": 258.08,
          "en": "way if you want to inspect it here you can use console.dir and now you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.08,
          "end": 260.42,
          "en": "get a inspectable javascript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.42,
          "end": 268.24,
          "en": "object so this is really the full dom element and this does not just work with html input elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.24,
          "end": 274.46,
          "en": "it works with any html element and your own components as well so we can also use a div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.46,
          "end": 281.98,
          "en": "instead and bind this to someDiv which of course is a variable I have yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 281.98,
          "end": 283.14,
          "en": "to add so here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.78,
          "end": 291.2,
          "en": "someDiv and now for simplicity when we click saveData I can now also console.dir",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 292.84000000000003,
          "end": 298.44,
          "en": "someDiv so it's the same button as before but now I'm binding this here this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 298.44,
          "end": 299.6,
          "en": "div to the someDiv",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 300.34,
          "end": 305.68,
          "en": "variable and therefore I can now interact with the div and inspect it and do whatever I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 305.68,
          "end": 310.46,
          "en": "again changing something there is not recommended you should always do that with the help of Svelte's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 310.46,
          "end": 314.52,
          "en": "normal syntax, but reading values from it can be really useful.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
